  input-precision-validation: LANDED 2026-07-10 with
    missing-incorporate-matrix-interface (de67cbb). dbartsData warns
    when range(y)/max(abs(y)) < 1e-10 (0/0 guarded); deliberately NO
    cardinality check backs it up - a genuine double-precision
    collapse always trips the ratio, while anything cardinality-only
    is well-separated legitimate discrete data (subsumption argument
    in small-validation-fixes.md). GP predict-vs-recorded-fit note
    landed in man/dbartsPriors.Rd and gp-leaves.md.
  multi-forest-models: multinomial, heteroscedastic, hurdle - the BCF
    two-forest machinery (forest-split-bcf, complete at c9fd2fe) is
    the template; one design note each when picked. Review-6
    prerequisites: forest-combiner FIRST (all three bend on it);
    heteroscedastic additionally needs a fourth leaf kind
    (multiplicative-positive, non-integrable) plus the non-conjugate
    MoveStrategy the design anticipated but never built, and a
    decision on per-observation residual variance (fold into the
    workingWeights channel vs a sigma vector).
  chi-default-research: staged by VD 2026-07-08 alongside the
    chi-hyperprior-df fix. The chi(1.25, Inf) binary default came
    from a simulation showing good binary-outcome performance; with
    the label now honest (chi(1.5)), re-derive the default from
    evidence. PART 1 DONE (roadmap-survey rider, 2026-07-10,
    detailed table in roadmap-survey.md): dbarts is the ONLY
    package with a hyperprior-on-k binary default; the field is
    fixed k=2 (BART, bartMachine, bartz), SoftBart alone at fixed
    k=1 (unexplained), stochtree samples leaf VARIANCE via IG (not
    k), pymc-bart exposes no knob; NO published rationale anywhere
    for a non-2 default. PART 2 remains: a broad simulation over
    binary scenarios (n, p, prevalence, signal strength/sparsity,
    friedman + linear + interaction DGPs) comparing k defaults and
    chi hyperprior settings on held-out log-loss, AUC, calibration,
    and interval coverage - now also deciding the chi-k-runaway
    remedy's default-scale half and rbart_vi's k default (interface
    taste call T5). Output: a design note + recommendation; any
    default change is its own posterior-changing item with VD's
    sign-off.
  bcf-glue-sigma-calibration: RESOLVED 2026-07-10 as H-MIX (slow
    mixing), not a defect - the chain-length experiment (three
    points spanning 8.3x: thin 120/360/1000, R=200, L=150) shows
    the sigma rank bias shrinking monotonically into PASS (rank
    mean 65.8 -> 67.8 -> 69.7 toward 75; ecdf 0.113 -> 0.107 ->
    0.065 vs band 0.092; chisqP 0.0002 -> 0.105 -> 0.617), where a
    defect would plateau; all controls pass at every point. The
    glue-scaled forest-update path is exonerated: the stationary
    distribution is correct within SBC resolution. Mechanism
    measured directly: sigma and the (a, mu) ridge co-relax with
    IACT scaling steeply in the prognostic amplitude |a0| (IACT 4
    at a0 ~ 0 to ~5000-6000 sweeps at |a0| ~ 7-13, the Cauchy(0,2)
    tail), so fixed thinning leaves the strong-signal minority
    correlated and sigma biased high in finite chains. Remedy
    routed to bcf-ridge-interweaving (below). Full record in
    sbc-calibration.md; artifacts in the session tmp.
  bcf-ridge-interweaving: LANDED 2026-07-10 (9617c94) as a mixing
    win; acceptance RE-SCOPED. The a-ridge rescale (c^2 ~
    GIG((L-1)/2, M/leafVar, a0^2/aVariance) after drawGlue;
    aVariance held - refreshing it measurably hurt mixing) is
    posterior-preserving (bcf-exact + bcf-exact-weak PASS),
    off-path bit-identical, ~3.9%/sweep, |a| IACT 2.5x better.
    New ext_rng_simulateGeneralizedInverseGaussian (Dagpunar
    noshift ROU, moment-tested) in external. BUT the thin=120
    sigma SBC flag persists in BOTH base and new builds at R=400
    (sigma rank mean ~67-69/75), and sigma IACT (~40) << thin, so
    the residual is NOT (a, mu) autocorrelation - see
    bcf-sigma-residual.
  bcf-sigma-residual: successor to bcf-glue-sigma-calibration
    (2026-07-10). At R=400 SBC both pre- and post-interweave
    builds flag sigma (rank mean ~67-69/75, ecdf ~0.10 vs band
    0.066) at thin=120 on the n=200 glue-on config; the a-ridge
    move did not clear it and sigma's marginal IACT is well under
    the thinning, so the bias rides another slow mode or a burn
    transient. PRIME SUSPECT: the treatment-side (b0, b1,
    tau-amplitude) scale ridge (b0/b1 ~ N(0, 1/2), tau forest;
    same non-identifiability as the a-ridge). Next steps: (1)
    derive the analogous b-ridge interweave (the a-move memo in
    bcf-ridge-interweaving.md is the template; GIG machinery now
    ships); (2) a fixed-b control SBC (updateB off) to localize,
    mirroring A4c; (3) a burn-only sweep to split transient from
    autocorrelation. The A4e thin=1000 PASS is consistent with a
    long transient (burn scales with thin in that design).

