  c-api-growth: LANDED 2026-07-10 (0254f10 output surface,
    2d09768 state format; plan + design-change record in
    c-api-growth.md). VD revised the decided design mid-flight:
    since nothing on CRAN links against the unreleased 1.0-0
    header, there is NO second entry point - dbarts_results itself
    is size-first (leading caller-set structSize; the library
    fills a field only when present-by-size and non-null; fields
    append monotonically below a marked boundary and bump
    DBARTS_C_API_VERSION, which stays 1 at introduction). Layout
    locked by static asserts; write guard proven by a compiled
    C-consumer canary with poisoned out-of-bounds slots. State
    format: version stamp demoted to an encoding floor
    (minReadableStateFormatVersion = 3) over the by-name block
    reader; required blocks refused BY NAME (missing vs
    malformed); append-only registry rule in public-surface.md.
    Absorbs flat-format-v2. LOCKSTEP ACTION at 1.0-0: stan4bart's
    port adds r.structSize = sizeof r at its dbarts_results
    allocations. The engine-side logLikelihood channel was
    deferred (per-family producer needs a new response-model
    virtual + group plumbing) - append it when built; the
    boundary comment marks the spot.
