  weighted-binary: memo findings (2026-07-10, issue #79): the
    semantics are ALREADY RESOLVED in the bartcore cutover - probit
    refuses weights (all-1 dropped for SuperLearner), logistic does
    exact integer frequency weights via summed PG(1, psi) draws
    (empirically identical to row replication, cor = 1.0), docs
    state all three families' meanings; BART/bartMachine offer no
    weighted binary at all. ONE residual defect, READY TO
    IMPLEMENT: sampleFromPPD (R/generics.R ~916-933) still draws
    rbinom(n, 1, ev) * w - a degenerate {0, w} two-point whose mean
    is right by luck but whose intervals are wrong; the coherent
    draw for a count-w row is rbinom(n, size = w, prob = ev).
    PPD FIX LANDED 2026-07-10 (da7b659): sampleFromPPD now draws
    rbinom(n, size = w, prob = ev) in both the matrix and array
    branches (recycling verified per fill order), bart.Rd
    documents binomial(w, p) counts, and the weighted-binary
    regression tests #79 noted were missing now exist
    (test-weighted-binary-ppd.R). #79's last live path is closed.
    FUTURE (unchanged, post 1.0): integer-weight probit via
    replicated latents; arbitrary real weights need a real-shape
    PG sampler (IPW is a pseudo-likelihood trap).
  within-chain-threading: previously assessed-and-deferred pending
    n >= 1e5 workloads, now confirmed common. Deterministic fixed-block
    reductions preserve thread-count invariance; the measurement
    interacts with hot-layer-u8 (same DRAM-bound regime) and competes
    with blocked-jacobi-trees as the mechanism.
  x86-simd: three linalg SSE2/AVX bodies are scalar with intrinsics
    commented out (predates the rewrite; the originals used
    non-temporal stores autovectorization cannot emit) - measure on
    x86, restore or delete; add misc_setIndexedVectorToConstant to the
    dispatch table; SSR SIMD leaf; Windows-arm64 NEON config.

release (deferred; the one ordered procedure, run when VD triggers it)
  note: the schedule/dispatch-only workflows (equivalence, rchk,
